      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wait this is not even modified after the constructor right ? Why is it not final, can you guarantee it will only ever be accessed on the same thread that initialized it ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 207,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 207,
        "endChar": 45
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fd5e9720_0c9cdb8b",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please don\u0027t duplicate the code you\u0027ve written in TetheringConfiguration. You can just read the field from there if you initialize this after the configuration has been read.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "612099d7_b00e880c",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 241,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this works – you\u0027re initializing this only once, but the resource can change at run time (which is why we have updateConfiguration). This happens for example when the SIM card is changed and the carrier config is updated.\n\nI think it should simply be a function in TetheringConfiguration. If you think evaluating this every time is too slow, make it a final boolean inside TetheringConfiguration.\n\nAlso this sounds like it contains whether the phone is *currently* tethering p2p. This is about support, right ? I suggest mIsWifiP2LegacyTetheringSupported.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 241,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 241,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4a254af_fe928bc8",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Likewise you\u0027ll have to make sure this is correct when the configuration changes. I think the simplest way to do that is to simply always add this action to the filter – you can notice other filters don\u0027t bother checking whether the regexp is empty. After all, if it\u0027s not supported, you don\u0027t expect to see this action at all (and if you do see it you return immediately anyway).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 308,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 308,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af5cf5c0_77cbe686",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this a protected broadcast ? If not, do we want to take any steps to avoid random apps sending that to the system ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 308,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 308,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "37996ebd_44f29c53",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 808,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s do this first before reading the parcelables. Likewise with p2pInfo, let\u0027s not read the group if the info is null",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 808,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 808,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45e6455d_0b0bab54",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 815,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For my education, what is the difference between p2pInfo.isGroupOwner and group.isGroupOwner() ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 815,
        "startChar": 34,
        "endLine": 815,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b5f2237c_db4a7bbb",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 821,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How do you plan to order this with respect to the events that update mTetherStates ? I get that this is under mutual exclusion so you\u0027ll always see a state that is consistent, but I don\u0027t think it\u0027s enough here. You actually need to have the state updated before this method runs.\n\nHowever IIUC the state is updated in response to an netd event and this method is called as a response to a broadcast, and either of these can be arbitrarily delayed. How do you make sure the broadcast always comes only after the state has been updated ?\n\nMark : isn\u0027t this the reason the current state is passed inside the intent in handleWifiAction ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 821,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 821,
        "endChar": 86
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47181448_03e75110",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 821,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T10:15:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The current state in handleWifiAction just indicate the state of wifi. It don\u0027t reflect tethering\u0027s state. But this intent base architecture seems would have race problem. \nIn current architecture, p2p and tethering run at different threads. And they don\u0027t check each other synchronously. If p2p off/on very quickly, it seems below flow may happen.\nwifi p2p enable in wifi\u0027s code --\u003ep2p enable intent--\u003e tethering enable --\u003e\nwifi p2p disable in wifi --\u003e wifi p2p quickly enable in wifi again --\u003ep2p disable intent--\u003e tethering disable --\u003ep2p enable intent--\u003e tethering enable.\n\nFor handleWifiAction(wifi tethering), I plan to replace intent as SoftApCallback. But p2p seems just rely on intent. If p2p also have callback, it would be better to pass p2p\u0027s state via callback.",
      "parentUuid": "b5f2237c_db4a7bbb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 821,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 821,
        "endChar": 86
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da3920d3_e402b7fb",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 825,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How strong is your guarantee that this will never overlap the possible interface names for regular wifi tethering ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 825,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 825,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d078f3c2_6717cc51",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 877,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T07:29:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rather than doing this, I think it\u0027s better to move it up. disableWifiIpServingLocked only has one caller : you could move it immediately before the call.\nBetter yet, keep this method for the common code, and have a disableWifiIpServingLocked method that just says mWifiTetherRequested\u003dfalse;commonCode(); and also a disableP2PServingLocked method that only calls the common code.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 877,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 877,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
